{"event_type":"review","id":"9a31f2ff07693730929954f3c97fd427337479b206c3e553c23667a94d6d1646","occurred_at":"2026-11-06T04:06:18Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/080cc21e917de7465d08db690c8c23948a3c2424bda6c4cb00e38c0b9255651a","sha256":"080cc21e917de7465d08db690c8c23948a3c2424bda6c4cb00e38c0b9255651a"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b9310ddd8880fd3d4c27a51f0684ee47d0bb025c75a31bd937274441b80eef6b","sha256":"b9310ddd8880fd3d4c27a51f0684ee47d0bb025c75a31bd937274441b80eef6b"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b0f9e3947dd15991e65f3e06a24ef6c31cfe6ab03e11cdf69dfc91acd6c5455c","sha256":"b0f9e3947dd15991e65f3e06a24ef6c31cfe6ab03e11cdf69dfc91acd6c5455c"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/00dd97177c3f8b2534f586f4cd27ff15fb80c440f5f0692c0a961a513379f9ae","sha256":"00dd97177c3f8b2534f586f4cd27ff15fb80c440f5f0692c0a961a513379f9ae"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/cfdd92e162d9a8fb685a87784474cd7ba023646c82ed0967393920b27227b420","sha256":"cfdd92e162d9a8fb685a87784474cd7ba023646c82ed0967393920b27227b420"}],"attempt_id":"30280dab728f8aa5d3115317428b9bf1bee6062d6191f5a893c40b8522e181c5:0:1","base":"2efaeb4392913f45f3d4005c92d5acdaf3f87fee","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"ef8cf46c4a884e41fc66fc72dfb6c1c1611cdb55","body":"**Isolate the usage-output env vars in the `peak-aware driver credential` describe block.**\n\nThis block never clears `GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY` or `SWEEP_USAGE_OUT`. The tests at Lines 1213-1254, 1269-1300 and 1302-1339 run `main()` to completion, so `appendStepSummaryTable` and `writeSweepUsageFile` read both variables from the real environment. `GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY` is set on GitHub Actions runners. A CI test run would therefore append a fake \"Sweep token usage\" table to the real job summary. The `SWEEP_USAGE_OUT` write would also be live if the workflow exports it.\n\nThe sibling `main — usage reporting` block already stubs both variables in `setup()`. Clear them in a `beforeEach` here.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-describe('main — peak-aware driver credential (fail closed)', () => {\n-  const originalArgv = process.argv;\n-  afterEach(() => {\n+describe('main — peak-aware driver credential (fail closed)', () => {\n+  const originalArgv = process.argv;\n+  beforeEach(() => {\n+    vi.stubEnv('GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY', '');\n+    vi.stubEnv('SWEEP_USAGE_OUT', '');\n+  });\n+  afterEach(() => {\n```\n\nAdd `beforeEach` to the `vitest` import on Line 75.\n</details>\n\nAs per path instructions for `test/**`: prefer assertions and fixtures that exercise intended behavior. Tests must not depend on ambient CI environment state.","id":"b803e5ffdb0a530a510d8a5961fa956d9f7b48479f2fe59b0d56028d44f47292","intervals":[],"path":"test/selfhost/self-review-loop.test.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Isolate the usage-output env vars in the `peak-aware driver credential` describe block."}],"head":"30e65d7258a808b47bb51a7143d3a39330508b55","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"c015ea45841290ad326f88a796d1d4308def8904","intervals":[[11,11],[71,73]],"path":"docs/inventory-crosscheck.md"},{"blob":"ada7eb23536485b8cb9b7649f25db83fa5e46c2a","intervals":[[9,9],[12,15],[76,78],[96,98],[104,105],[108,109],[111,112],[114,116],[152,307],[402,407],[463,483],[486,488],[493,499],[556,563],[671,674],[768,817],[910,916],[936,937],[981,1057],[1078,1083],[1087,1089],[1105,1107],[1109,1198],[1200,1200],[1231,1231],[1241,1241],[1248,1248],[1421,1431],[1434,1441],[1444,1447],[1449,1453],[1461,1465],[1469,1478],[1550,1556],[1558,1602],[1604,1604],[1663,1664],[1677,1677],[1689,1689],[1709,1710]],"path":"src/plans/review-l